Is facet is important to you? Social Potency score have to report each factor score instead general score?
Why are you split data in item response theory perspectives? Under the Model-based approach may not important split randomly. Because the IRT is not sample-based approach. If you had the representative sampling, you can apply item parameters to another sample.
Did you check item fit statistic in one-factor solution? In the IRT perspectives, validity can justification by item fit statistics. In this situation, the short scale may not need testlets.
Best,
Seongho

